        <mxCell id="note" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;fillColor=#f5f5f5;fontColor=#333333;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=12;" value="&lt;b&gt;How to read&lt;/b&gt;: boxes are grouped by where each part runs. Everything inside &quot;SAE A computer&quot; is one process; the database is a file. Links to the KME, other SAEs and to the keychain all use mutual TLS;&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;TLS to SAEs and Keychain uses PQC while TLS to KME uses only Classical algorithms.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;SAE B is set up the same way as SAE A.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
